        "caption": "Yosemite Falls is the highest waterfall in Yosemite National Park, dropping a total of 2,425 feet (739 m) from the top of the upper fall to the base of the lower fall. \nThe Upper falls drop 1430 feet, the Lower falls 320 feet and in between are a series of smaller falls which are difficult to see from the valley.\n\nHere both parts of the main falls can be seen.",
